{"id":"2d699a9437790a33","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-brouwer.md","title":"Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem","display":"df-brouwer — Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-brouwer","aliases":["58-df-brouwer","Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem"],"display":"df-brouwer — Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-brouwer"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-brouwer</span><span>Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-brouwer — Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b2e63b755a37f1dc\" href=\"?note=b2e63b755a37f1dc\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md\">../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n,f\\in V\">\\(n,f\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D^n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|\\leq1\\}\">\\(D^n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|\\leq1\\}\\)</span> (closed unit ball)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{D^n}=\\{U\\cap D^n:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\}\">\\(\\tau_{D^n}=\\{U\\cap D^n:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\}\\)</span> (the Euclidean subspace topology)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S\\)</span> (continuous-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b2e63b755a37f1dc\" href=\"?note=b2e63b755a37f1dc\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md\">../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BrouwerFPT}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{BrouwerFPT}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (property defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brouwer} \\vdash \\mathrm{BrouwerFPT}_S(n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\\forall f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(f,D^n,\\tau_{D^n},D^n,\\tau_{D^n})\\to\\exists x\\in D^n\\;(f(x)=x)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brouwer} \\vdash \\mathrm{BrouwerFPT}_S(n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\\forall f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(f,D^n,\\tau_{D^n},D^n,\\tau_{D^n})\\to\\exists x\\in D^n\\;(f(x)=x)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The continuous-map call includes the source and target topologies required by its five-argument upstream signature.</li>\n<li>Brouwer: every continuous self-map of the Euclidean closed ball has a fixed point.</li>\n<li>The compact-convex and no-retraction formulations are equivalent consequences, not separate definition clauses here.</li>\n<li>Retraction: no continuous retraction of ball to sphere</li>\n<li>Topological degree: counts fixed points for regular values</li>\n<li>Applications: Nash equilibrium, Kakutani fixed point theorem</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Milnor, Topology from the Differentiable Viewpoint</li>\n<li>Lee, Introduction to Topological Manifolds</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"b2e63b755a37f1dc","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"b2e63b755a37f1dc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S$ (continuous-function predicate, see [[../batch17/58-df-continuous-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n,f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"D^n=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^n:\\|x\\|\\leq1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{D^n}=\\{U\\cap D^n:U\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BrouwerFPT}_S\\subseteq V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}brouwer} \\vdash \\mathrm{BrouwerFPT}_S(n)\\leftrightarrow n\\in\\omega\\land\\forall f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{ContinuousFunction}_S(f,D^n,\\tau_{D^n},D^n,\\tau_{D^n})\\to\\exists x\\in D^n\\;(f(x)=x)\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1518,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-217","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-brouwer.md|58-df-brouwer]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["b2e63b755a37f1dc"]}